[
  {
    "key": "imitation-of-christ/original-en/ch76",
    "group": "alignment",
    "title": "Chapter 39",
    "text_paragraph_count": 6,
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "index": 0,
        "file": "p0.mp3",
        "path": "audio/imitation-of-christ/original-en/ch76/p0.mp3",
        "sha256": "3cf070c4692c1a0648b525120c22e393646672dbeabbe984d4a77402704f7f4e",
        "bytes": 51117,
        "duration": 3.1460416666666666,
        "manifest_duration": 3.1,
        "text": "That man must not be immersed in business"
      },
      {
        "index": 1,
        "file": "p1.mp3",
        "path": "audio/imitation-of-christ/original-en/ch76/p1.mp3",
        "sha256": "3dd3d50944fa557cee7a7839bea0938b26d6a11e4e0da4fa417aa60291181b00",
        "bytes": 159021,
        "duration": 9.896041666666667,
        "manifest_duration": 9.85,
        "text": "“My Son, always commit thy cause to Me; I will dispose it aright in due time. Wait for My arrangement of it, and then thou shalt find it for thy profit.”"
      },
      {
        "index": 2,
        "file": "p2.mp3",
        "path": "audio/imitation-of-christ/original-en/ch76/p2.mp3",
        "sha256": "3608a6a03b82636a03e2e576d659a36a96522eeba070c89d2d2d57a3fce29404",
        "bytes": 221613,
        "duration": 13.821041666666668,
        "manifest_duration": 13.78,
        "text": "2. O Lord, right freely I commit all things to Thee; for my planning can profit but little. Oh that I did not dwell so much on future events, but could offer myself altogether to Thy pleasures without delay."
      },
      {
        "index": 3,
        "file": "p3.mp3",
        "path": "audio/imitation-of-christ/original-en/ch76/p3.mp3",
        "sha256": "84fe03ddb038959b96b01a79be4190cae9ece9d8b13b9a622a5d5b4ca1b9e14a",
        "bytes": 326445,
        "duration": 20.371041666666667,
        "manifest_duration": 20.32,
        "text": "3. “My Son, a man often striveth vehemently after somewhat which he desireth; but when he hath obtained it he beginneth to be of another mind, because his affections towards it are not lasting, but rather rush on from one thing to another. Therefore it is not really a small thing, when in small things we resist self.”"
      },
      {
        "index": 4,
        "file": "p4.mp3",
        "path": "audio/imitation-of-christ/original-en/ch76/p4.mp3",
        "sha256": "8e3dd14ae69bada1370d84f8adc736ffdf75f31e91a9d6f232e54dd0f2a8f68d",
        "bytes": 367917,
        "duration": 22.946041666666666,
        "manifest_duration": 22.9,
        "text": "4. The true progress of man lieth in self-denial, and a man who denieth himself is free and safe. But the old enemy, opposer of all good things, ceaseth not from temptation; but day and night setteth his wicked snares, if haply he may be able to entrap the unwary. Watch and pray, saith the Lord, lest ye enter into temptation.(1)"
      },
      {
        "index": 5,
        "file": "p5.mp3",
        "path": "audio/imitation-of-christ/original-en/ch76/p5.mp3",
        "sha256": "47fc677d00ea3c16f85d8c081474f4c371308e07338b9d8735eeb3f497307ca7",
        "bytes": 59949,
        "duration": 3.696041666666667,
        "manifest_duration": 3.65,
        "text": "(1) Matthew xxvi. 41."
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "key": "king-lear/original-en/ch3",
    "group": "alignment",
    "title": "Act 1, Scene 3 — A Room in the Duke of Albany’s Palace",
    "text_paragraph_count": 10,
    "paragraphs": [
      {
        "index": 0,
        "file": "p0.mp3",
        "path": "audio/king-lear/original-en/ch3/p0.mp3",
        "sha256": "5495ffd77be07195ada213cdd74b937ee45515fbbbbacebb7b2431619ecd0566",
        "bytes": 42669,
        "duration": 2.6210416666666667,
        "manifest_duration": 2.64,
        "text": "Enter Goneril and Oswald."
      },
      {
        "index": 1,
        "file": "p1.mp3",
        "path": "audio/king-lear/original-en/ch3/p1.mp3",
        "sha256": "5c590f0ec076bf2df43e1e21e57bf3ef15509283823a437600592f750eec6538",
        "bytes": 77229,
        "duration": 4.7960416666666665,
        "manifest_duration": 4.8,
        "text": "GONERIL. Did my father strike my gentleman for chiding of his fool?"
      },
      {
        "index": 2,
        "file": "p2.mp3",
        "path": "audio/king-lear/original-en/ch3/p2.mp3",
        "sha256": "3f853586e90a721c61fef83d7879e780f8a285e8a94d48ce4865ba9e0a97f39b",
        "bytes": 38445,
        "duration": 2.3710416666666667,
        "manifest_duration": 2.376,
        "text": "OSWALD. Ay, madam."
      },
      {
        "index": 3,
        "file": "p3.mp3",
        "path": "audio/king-lear/original-en/ch3/p3.mp3",
        "sha256": "1acf56835d3691aeed9e561e122fff0c75fa611803c978f0f5a85be892e2fbff",
        "bytes": 364461,
        "duration": 22.746041666666667,
        "manifest_duration": 22.752,
        "text": "GONERIL. By day and night, he wrongs me; every hour He flashes into one gross crime or other, That sets us all at odds; I’ll not endure it: His knights grow riotous, and himself upbraids us On every trifle. When he returns from hunting, I will not speak with him; say I am sick. If you come slack of former services, You shall do well; the fault of it I’ll answer."
      },
      {
        "index": 4,
        "file": "p4.mp3",
        "path": "audio/king-lear/original-en/ch3/p4.mp3",
        "sha256": "c1a1ebece386aff8b35822b971d2a9798141d637ca5b7322cc4c9d68223a9d1a",
        "bytes": 28461,
        "duration": 1.7460416666666667,
        "manifest_duration": 1.752,
        "text": "[_Horns within._]"
      },
      {
        "index": 5,
        "file": "p5.mp3",
        "path": "audio/king-lear/original-en/ch3/p5.mp3",
        "sha256": "9dd7242f1108d24aa1780b01d6e51d9580cea113019534030baca7c1dc7276b8",
        "bytes": 54957,
        "duration": 3.3960416666666666,
        "manifest_duration": 3.408,
        "text": "OSWALD. He’s coming, madam; I hear him."
      },
      {
        "index": 6,
        "file": "p6.mp3",
        "path": "audio/king-lear/original-en/ch3/p6.mp3",
        "sha256": "039e1eb69f042edd3fad8921d9bd99a5d71400f13513eb3bce348beb9e8420c5",
        "bytes": 409773,
        "duration": 25.571041666666666,
        "manifest_duration": 25.584,
        "text": "GONERIL. Put on what weary negligence you please, You and your fellows; I’d have it come to question: If he distaste it, let him to our sister, Whose mind and mine, I know, in that are one, Not to be overruled. Idle old man, That still would manage those authorities That he hath given away! Now, by my life, Old fools are babes again; and must be us’d With checks as flatteries, when they are seen abus’d. Remember what I have said."
      },
      {
        "index": 7,
        "file": "p7.mp3",
        "path": "audio/king-lear/original-en/ch3/p7.mp3",
        "sha256": "ead51a68ea14c06ebea5475dbee869c9ffa9fcf1f30c15f0e4d865a9ad2952a9",
        "bytes": 44973,
        "duration": 2.7710416666666666,
        "manifest_duration": 2.784,
        "text": "OSWALD. Very well, madam."
      },
      {
        "index": 8,
        "file": "p8.mp3",
        "path": "audio/king-lear/original-en/ch3/p8.mp3",
        "sha256": "d80c0e74ef3b01f49478ddae533dea1a02cb7257f987a2b21cb315386e7931e2",
        "bytes": 252333,
        "duration": 15.721041666666668,
        "manifest_duration": 15.744,
        "text": "GONERIL. And let his knights have colder looks among you; What grows of it, no matter; advise your fellows so; I would breed from hence occasions, and I shall, That I may speak. I’ll write straight to my sister To hold my very course. Prepare for dinner."
      },
      {
        "index": 9,
        "file": "p9.mp3",
        "path": "audio/king-lear/original-en/ch3/p9.mp3",
        "sha256": "7802beea1fea72119611f32e6544d44100ee127fd8bcdcace2dabe57a935091c",
        "bytes": 26541,
        "duration": 1.6210416666666667,
        "manifest_duration": 1.632,
        "text": "[_Exeunt._]"
      }
    ]
  }
]